# One rule for line endings on every machine: text files are LF in the repo and in the working copy.
# Why: with Windows autocrlf checkouts, files written with LF (by Linux/cloud sessions or copied over) showed up
# as modified although their content was the same.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Git already detects these as binary (88 font files); said here so it never touches their bytes.
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
